why: Kirill counted 25 blocks of 72 saying "this function" and asked for synonyms, or none; on a declaration with a body the act's subject is the domain thing with an active verb where there is one, as "an escrow requirement goes to `legacyLedgerKeys` first", then a role noun, then this function
labelled: 2026-09-29
--- code
export async function getSettlementClaim(requirement: SettlementRequirement): Promise<LedgerClaim> {
  const first = requirement.clearing === Clearing.Escrow ? askLegacyLedgerKeys : askStandardApi;
  const second = first === askLegacyLedgerKeys ? askStandardApi : askLegacyLedgerKeys;
  const claim = await first(requirement);
  return claim === LedgerClaim.Unknown ? second(requirement) : claim;
}
--- facts
On older ledgers `requestSettlementAccess` rejects escrow, so this function asks `legacyLedgerKeys` first about an escrow requirement.
`legacyLedgerKeys` supports escrow only, so this function asks the standard API first about any other clearing.
